Priorities: Context

Purpose:
  Defines context element priority levels and selection rules.

PriorityLevels:
  P0:
    Description: mandatory
    Examples:
      - task itself
      - parent task
      - required skill
      - affected source
  P1:
    Description: strongly relevant
    Examples:
      - related test
      - architecture
      - security skill
  P2:
    Description: useful
    Examples:
      - general documentation
      - related incidents
      - observability
  P3:
    Description: optional
    Examples:
      - peripheral docs
      - unrelated modules
  P4:
    Description: background
    Examples:
      - unrelated domains
      - unrelated infrastructure

SelectionRules:
  [PR1]  P0 MUST always be loaded.
  [PR2]  P1 MUST be loaded if within context budget.
  [PR3]  P2 MAY be loaded if context budget allows.
  [PR4]  P3 and P4 MUST NOT be loaded unless explicitly requested.
  [PR5]  If context budget exceeded, lower priority items are dropped
          before higher priority items.

State: +
  